#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:1
msgid ""
"<div class=\"warning\">\n"
"WARNING: Current Windows support is experimental.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:5
msgid "Source Installation on Windows 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:7
msgid ""
"Currently, `ign-gazebo` and `ign-launch` are not supported on Windows 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:9
msgid ""
"Additionally, command line tools, DART physics engine, and GUI capabilities "
"are not currently supported in Windows. These functionalities correspond to "
"the currently building packages `ign-tools`, `ign-physics`, and `ign-gui`, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:13
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:15
msgid ""
"You will still be able to use `TPE` as a physics engine (see [here](https://"
"gazebosim.org/api/physics/2.2/physicsplugin.html) for more information on "
"`TPE`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:18
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:20
msgid ""
"Install a [Conda package management system](https://docs.conda.io/projects/"
"conda/en/latest/user-guide/install/download.html). Miniconda suffices. You "
"will likely want to check the box to add `conda` to your `PATH` during the "
"installation process so that you won't have to do this step manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:24
msgid ""
"Install [Visual Studio 2019](https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/). "
"The Community version is free for students, open-source developers, and "
"personal development. Check \"Desktop development with C++\" in the "
"Workloads tab, and uncheck \"C++ Cmake Tools.\" We will install cmake via "
"Conda."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:29
msgid ""
"Open a Visual Studio Command Prompt (search for \"x64 Native Tools Command "
"Prompt for VS 2019\" in the Windows search field near the Windows button). "
"Optionally, right-click and pin to the task bar for quick access in the "
"future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:33
msgid ""
"If you did not add Conda to your `PATH` environment variable during Conda "
"installation,   you may need to navigate to the location of `condabin` in "
"order to use the `conda` command.   To find `condabin`, search for "
"\"Anaconda Prompt\" in the Windows search field near the   Windows button, "
"open it, run `where conda`, and look for a line containing the directory "
"`condabin`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:38
msgid ""
"Navigate to your `condabin`, if necessary, and then create and activate a "
"Conda environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:39
msgid ""
"conda create -n ign-ws\n"
"conda activate ign-ws\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:44
msgid ""
"Once you have activate an environment, a prefix like `(ign-ws)` will be "
"prepended to   your prompt, and you can use the `conda` command outside of "
"the `condabin` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:47
msgid "You can use `conda info --envs` to see all of your environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:49
msgid "To remove an environment, use `conda env remove --name <env_name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:51
msgid "Install dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:53
msgid ""
"conda install cmake git vcstool curl pkg-config ^\n"
"colcon-common-extensions eigen freeimage gts ^\n"
"glib dlfcn-win32 ffmpeg ruby tinyxml2 tinyxml ^\n"
"protobuf urdfdom zeromq cppzmq ogre jsoncpp ^\n"
"libzip qt --channel conda-forge\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:61
msgid ""
"Navigate to where you would like to build the library, create and enter your "
"workspace directory, create the `src` directory which will contain the "
"Ignition source code, and then clone the repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:63
msgid ""
"mkdir ign-ws\n"
"cd ign-ws\n"
"curl -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ignition-tooling/gazebodistro/"
"master/collection-dome.yaml\n"
"mkdir src\n"
"vcs import src < collection-dome.yaml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:71
msgid "Building the Ignition Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:73
msgid ""
"Once the compiler and all the sources are in place it is time to compile "
"them. Start the procedure by navigating to your workspace and listing the "
"packages recognized by `colcon`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:77
msgid "colcon graph\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:81
msgid ""
"`colcon graph` should list the Ignition libraries with an [interdependency "
"diagram](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/verb/graph."
"html#example-output). If that is the case, then you are ready to build the "
"whole set of libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:85
msgid ""
"colcon build --cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF --merge-install --packages-up-"
"to ignition-gazebo4\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:88
msgid "Tests are turned off as they are not currently supported on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:90
msgid ""
"**Note:** All of the Ignition packages up to, but not including `ign-gazebo` "
"are currently building.  The above command should successfully build all "
"packages except for `ign-gazebo`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:93
msgid "To build a specific package with all its dependent packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:95
msgid "colcon build --merge-install --packages-up-to PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:99
msgid "To build a single package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:101
msgid "colcon build --packages-select PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:105
msgid ""
"Visit [colcon documentation](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/#) to "
"view more `colcon` build and test options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:107
msgid "If there are no errors, all the binaries should be ready to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:109
msgid "Using the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:111
msgid "The workspace needs to be sourced every time a new terminal is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:113
msgid "Run the following command to source the workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:115
msgid "call install\\setup.bat\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:119
msgid ""
"This is the end of the source install instructions; head back to the "
"[Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Ignition!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:122
msgid "Uninstalling source-based install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:124
msgid ""
"A source-based install can be \"uninstalled\" using several methods, "
"depending on the results you want:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:127
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with `colcon` as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's `setup.bat`. This way, your environment will behave "
"as though there is no Ignition install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:132
msgid ""
"If, in addition to not wanting to use the libraries, you're also trying to "
"free up space, you can delete the entire workspace directory from within "
"your `conda` environment with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:136
msgid "rm -rf <workspace_name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:140
msgid ""
"If you want to keep the source code, you can remove the `install` / "
"`build` / `log` directories as desired, leaving the `src` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:143
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows_src.md:145
msgid "See [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting)"
msgstr ""
